<title>FRANCE: Axa seller of Suez shares in block.</title>
<headline>Axa seller of Suez shares in block.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer Axa sold 2,122,729 Suez shares on Wednesday, or 1.2 percent of the capital, in a block trade to a single buyer at a price of 253.19 francs, an AXA spokesman said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Axa and Suez refused to disclose the identity of the buyer.</p>
<p>According to the Axa spokesman, the sale was part of the routine portfolio management of the insurer's holdings and was done with the agreement of Suez.</p>
<p>He said Axa's direct stake in Suez was 6.35 percent but, including the stakes held through investment funds in which it has majority control, the overall holding was 6.69 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
